# Without this file, line endings depend on each contributor's core.autocrlf.
# That is not cosmetic here: the Homebrew formula and its golden fixture are
# compared byte-for-byte by scripts/sync_package_manifests.py --check and by the
# test suite, so a CRLF checkout made those comparisons fail on Windows while
# passing on Linux and macOS.
#
# Scoped deliberately to the files this affects. Normalising the whole tree
# (shell scripts in particular, where a CRLF shebang line fails with
# "bad interpreter: ...^M") is tracked in issue #4.

# Generated and byte-compared.
*.rb        text eol=lf
*.golden    text eol=lf
